1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,162
A submarine sank

2
00:00:01,162 --> 00:00:02,092
to the seabed.

3
00:00:02,228 --> 00:00:04,133
People were still alive inside.

4
00:00:04,330 --> 00:00:05,742
To reach them, rescuers

5
00:00:05,742 --> 00:00:06,392
had to open

6
00:00:06,392 --> 00:00:07,572
a hatch underwater.

7
00:00:07,684 --> 00:00:08,321
But how could they

8
00:00:08,321 --> 00:00:09,484
do that without flooding

9
00:00:09,484 --> 00:00:10,059
the people they

10
00:00:10,059 --> 00:00:11,001
came to save?

11
00:00:11,221 --> 00:00:13,591
May twenty-third, nineteen thirty-nine.

12
00:00:13,770 --> 00:00:15,224
Off the American coast,

13
00:00:15,292 --> 00:00:16,629
the new submarine Squalus

14
00:00:16,629 --> 00:00:17,860
begins a test dive.

15
00:00:18,030 --> 00:00:19,256
An air induction valve

16
00:00:19,256 --> 00:00:20,363
fails to close.

17
00:00:20,514 --> 00:00:21,955
Seawater pours in.

18
00:00:22,121 --> 00:00:23,860
The aft compartments flood.

19
00:00:24,039 --> 00:00:25,642
Twenty-six people die.

20
00:00:25,785 --> 00:00:26,812
The others manage to

21
00:00:26,812 --> 00:00:28,044
seal off the water.

22
00:00:28,264 --> 00:00:29,689
Thirty-three people are trapped

23
00:00:29,689 --> 00:00:30,819
below the surface.

24
00:00:30,968 --> 00:00:31,806
The depth: two

25
00:00:31,806 --> 00:00:33,336
hundred forty-three feet.

26
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:34,554
Then a steel rescue

27
00:00:34,554 --> 00:00:35,492
chamber is lowered

28
00:00:35,492 --> 00:00:36,622
toward the submarine.

29
00:00:36,815 --> 00:00:37,902
But simply placing it

30
00:00:37,902 --> 00:00:38,727
over the hatch will

31
00:00:38,727 --> 00:00:39,695
not be enough.

32
00:00:39,915 --> 00:00:41,002
A diver attaches

33
00:00:41,002 --> 00:00:41,932
a guide cable.

34
00:00:42,036 --> 00:00:43,111
The chamber is pulled

35
00:00:43,111 --> 00:00:44,341
down onto the hatch.

36
00:00:44,510 --> 00:00:45,585
A rubber ring forms

37
00:00:45,585 --> 00:00:46,548
a watertight seal

38
00:00:46,548 --> 00:00:47,540
against the hull.

39
00:00:47,666 --> 00:00:48,891
Water is removed from

40
00:00:48,891 --> 00:00:50,658
the chamber's lower compartment.

41
00:00:50,804 --> 00:00:51,891
A dry passage now

42
00:00:51,891 --> 00:00:53,321
connects the two vessels.

43
00:00:53,461 --> 00:00:54,249
Only then can

44
00:00:54,249 --> 00:00:55,291
the hatches open.

45
00:00:55,447 --> 00:00:56,934
People climb inside, and

46
00:00:56,934 --> 00:00:58,047
the chamber carries them

47
00:00:58,047 --> 00:00:59,089
toward the surface.

48
00:00:59,310 --> 00:01:00,780
It takes four trips.

49
00:01:00,918 --> 00:01:02,283
All thirty-three people who

50
00:01:02,283 --> 00:01:03,456
survived the flooding are

51
00:01:03,456 --> 00:01:04,517
brought up alive.

52
00:01:04,675 --> 00:01:05,491
It is the first

53
00:01:05,491 --> 00:01:06,677
rescue from a sunken

54
00:01:06,677 --> 00:01:08,478
submarine using this method.

55
00:01:08,528 --> 00:01:09,523
They could not escape

56
00:01:09,523 --> 00:01:10,278
on their own.

57
00:01:10,458 --> 00:01:11,784
So rescuers brought the

58
00:01:11,784 --> 00:01:13,050
way out down to them.
